{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Spun from 73d8-4871-1b49-4047 (brainy-convulsant-unicorn) and 551b-1a30-ac2b-4127 (sanidine-cilium-eland) during the 2026-08-30 error-code decision pass.\n\n## Problem\n`error_code_for` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`) maps the broad `LLMError` family to `llm_unavailable`. That over-claims an AI-provider outage for non-outage faults: the bare `LLMError` base, concrete LLM/workflow subclasses that are not in the provider-unavailability subtree, and the editor missing-bundle failure that currently raises a bare `WorkflowError`. This is the residual of origin 8a31-e1c3-cf31-4239's blanket mapping and the systematic completion of epic 3405-c0b7-0436-4b46's descriptiveness intent.\n\n## Operator decision\nThe latest DECISION NEEDED comment approves narrowing `llm_unavailable` to true LLM availability failures while preserving dbca AC3's compatibility contract: a genuine outage surfaced through the bare `WorkflowError` execute-wrapper contract still reads as `llm_unavailable`. The implementation keeps `isinstance(exc, LLMUnavailableError) -> llm_unavailable`, intentionally including `LLMConfigError` / prompt / reviewer configuration subclasses because those classes inherit from `LLMUnavailableError` and model missing LLM dependencies, credentials, or configuration. The implementation removes the broad catch-all for all other `LLMError` instances.\n\nThe split between dbca AC3 and the editor missing-bundle case is type-based, not message-based. The bare `WorkflowError` base remains `llm_unavailable` as the legacy execute-outage wrapper contract. The editor missing-bundle raise at `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:475` will stop using bare `WorkflowError`; it will raise a dedicated `WorkflowAssetsUnavailableError(WorkflowError)` with `error_code = \"command_failed\"`. That delivers 551b's ruled behavior without message sniffing and without changing the dbca AC3 bare-base contract. Do not add `environment_unready`.\n\nTicket 73d8-4871-1b49-4047 is folded into this sweep by giving `ExpressionError` an explicit `error_code = \"invalid_input\"`, matching prior bug 35ab-f0e0-3e4a-4b72 (unknown-step -> invalid_input) and dbca-97ac-ad96-4d6d (parse/lint -> invalid_input).\n\n## Implementation scope\nTouch `src/rebar/_errors.py`, `src/rebar/llm/errors.py`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py`, and tests. Enumerate every concrete subclass of `LLMError` across `src/rebar/llm/`, including `errors.py`, `findings.py`, `evals/eval.py`, `prompting/`, and `workflow/`, with Serena hierarchy/reference checks and a grep/string confirmation. Update the existing pinned contract tests that currently assert the blanket mapping: `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_error_code_taxonomy_contract.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llmrunner_error_codes_f75f_heldout.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_workflow_error_codes_35ab.py`, and `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_workflow_error_codes_dbca.py`.\n\nIntended mapping: `LLMUnavailableError` and its availability/config subtree -> `llm_unavailable`; bare `WorkflowError` base -> `llm_unavailable` for the preserved dbca execute-outage wrapper contract; `WorkflowAssetsUnavailableError` -> `command_failed`; `ExpressionError` -> `invalid_input`; workflow caller/authoring errors already classified as `invalid_input` stay there; every remaining non-availability LLM/findings/eval/snapshot subclass without an explicit `error_code` -> `command_failed`; bare `LLMError` base -> `command_failed`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `src/rebar/_errors.py` returns `llm_unavailable` for `LLMUnavailableError` / `LLMConfigError` availability errors and preserves bare `WorkflowError` base -> `llm_unavailable` for the dbca execute-outage compatibility contract; focused tests verify these mappings.\n- [x] A dedicated editor missing-bundle exception raised from `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:475` maps to `command_failed`, not `llm_unavailable`, and no message sniffing is used.\n- [x] The broad `LLMError` base and every non-availability `LLMError` subclass except the deliberately preserved bare `WorkflowError` base maps to an explicit `error_code` when present, otherwise `command_failed`; a parameterized taxonomy test covers the complete enumerated subclass set.\n- [x] `ExpressionError` maps to `invalid_input` via an explicit `error_code`, verified by a focused test and by the exhaustive taxonomy test.\n- [x] No `environment_unready` code is introduced; `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` remains consistent with the intentional taxonomy.\n\n## Testing\nRun the focused updated contract tests with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/interfaces/contracts/test_error_code_taxonomy_contract.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llmrunner_error_codes_f75f_heldout.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_workflow_error_codes_35ab.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_workflow_error_codes_dbca.py`, then `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` and `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`. After committing, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" rebar verify-commit-ticket HEAD`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788305428964398001,"uuid":"7bb9123a-22ea-4594-874c-af787fd90abf"}